  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ontong Java Adaptation and Resilience (OJAR) Programme, Solomon Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anglican Missions will work in partnership with the Anglican Church of Melanesia to enhance the resilience and well-being of communities on the remote atoll of Ontong Java, Solomon Islands, which faces existential threats from climate change, sea level rise, and natural disasters. The Activity will address three critical areas: sustainable agriculture, water and sanitation, and disaster preparedness to increase resilience to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
